{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the Canaanite, king of Arad, heard.</b> The ancients said that he is Sihon, and he is called the Canaanite because every Amorite is a Canaanite. And many said that Joshua wrote this pericope, and the proof is 'king of Arad' in the singular, and they found that the children of Judah called the place Hormah — yet they said nothing, for that place was originally called Zepheth, and this is the king of Arad. The truth is: two places, and there are many such in Scripture. 'And the king of Arad' in its plain sense is across the Jordan eastward. And this pericope is adjacent to the death of Aaron because Scripture recounted what happened at Mount Hor before they journeyed from there — and the proof is 'And the Canaanite, king of Arad, heard,' and after it 'And they journeyed from Mount Hor.' And if you ask what he heard — it is explicitly stated." "<b>For Israel came by the way of the Atharim.</b> האתרים: the alef is added, and the meaning is התרים את הארץ (spying out the land). Likewise the alef in אזרועך."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:37.479161990Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}